WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.520
Hello again, dear viewers.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.490
You’ve caught me during my break.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.490
What?

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.370
Even researchers at the SCP Foundation need
a little downtime now and then.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.059
And considering they revoked my playtime privileges
with The Living Lego and the Nerfing Gun after

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:17.980
the unfortunate incident in the Site-19 Break
Room, I’ve been downgraded to keeping myself

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.710
occupied with this little rubber ball.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.989
“I have a ball.

00:00:20.989 --> 00:00:22.880
Perhaps you'd like to bounce it,” they said.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.189
Seems innocent enough, doesn’t it?

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:29.489
Oh, have you learned nothing?

00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:35.070
Almost any object, even something as innocuous
as a Teddy Bear or a plastic paddling pool,

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.070
can hide secrets.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.440
Sure, any avid basketball fan will happily
tell you that ball is life.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.089
But sometimes, when you’re dealing with
anomalies, a ball can also… be death.

00:00:46.089 --> 00:00:51.750
Such is the case of SCP-018, also known as
The Super Ball.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:57.890
An anomaly so powerful that the Foundation
has even used it to help recontain SCP-682

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.170
during a breach.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.640
To the untrained observer, it really isn’t
much to look at.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.640
A small, red rubber ball, about six centimeters
in diameter, produced by the Wham-O company

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.020
in 1969.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.520
Yeah, we were as surprised as you to find
out that good ol’ Dr. Wondertainment had

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.570
nothing to do with this little number.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:21.570
You might also be surprised by just how extensive
the containment procedures are for SCP-018

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.840
- After all, it’s rare that a competently
non-sentient anomaly makes its way into the

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.420
Euclid class.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.640
This little rubber ball is kept in a specially-made
titanium-alloy metal restraint, submerged

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.850
in a dense polyethylene holding tank, filled
with a special endothermic compound that draws

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.750
the kinetic energy out of its surroundings.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:46.650
Anyone entering the chamber needs to wear
a unique kind of reinforced plate armor, and

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:52.420
if SCP-018 ever manages to escape its containment
tank, nearby personnel are advised to treat

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.610
it as they would an active shooter situation.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:02:00.050
Lock yourself in a nearby room, duck down
below any cover you can find, and wait for

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:03.880
armed containment units to show up and take
control of the situation.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:09.200
At this point, you probably have a lot of
questions, chief among them being: Why is

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.780
this children’s toy being given more security
precautions than most serial killers?

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.810
The ball was first discovered when a cleaning
and disposal company was hired to empty out

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.370
an old Wham-O warehouse of some defunct merchandise.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:25.500
One of the movers, Roy Fischler, embraced
his inner child when he saw a red, rubber

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.730
ball sitting among all the dusty boxes of
expired silly putty and broken remote control

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:31.730
robots.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.680
He thought to himself, “what’s the harm
in having a little fun here?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.390
It’s all going into the trash anyway.”

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:40.670
This would prove to be a terrible mistake
for all involved.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:47.210
The anomalous property of SCP-018 is the fact
that it’s able to bounce at 200% efficiency

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:52.780
every time it’s bounced, increasing at an
exponential rate with each bounce unless it’s

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.110
stopped by some equivalent force.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:00.270
So when Roy decided to toss that little red
ball onto the ground, he’d unleashed a destructive

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:05.570
force into that warehouse that was more powerful
than he ever could have imagined.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:10.380
With every bounce, the ball increased its
height and speed, ricocheting across the floor,

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.160
walls, and ceiling like a bullet run amok.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.040
And it was only just getting started.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.580
The workers hit the deck as the item that
would later be dubbed SCP-018 decided to put

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.530
the “ball” in “ballistic.”

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.280
It smashed light fixtures.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.440
Knocked over piles of boxes.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.810
Smashed through forklifts.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.190
When one worker tried to catch it, it left
a red-hot, ball-shaped hole in the middle

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.540
of his palm.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.069
It wasn’t long before the ball had built
up such speed that the warehouse could no

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:38.290
longer contain it.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:43.690
It blasted out of the wall and rocketed into
the nearby city, ready to cause more abject

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.910
chaos wherever it went.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.300
Windows were shattered.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.960
Street lights were annihilated.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.090
Cars crashed.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.980
Thankfully, no humans were killed by the rampaging
rubber menace, but in total five people were

00:03:54.980 --> 00:04:00.620
injured - And one unfortunate pigeon was utterly
obliterated on impact.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:05.550
It went on for several days, with the ball
reaching over 100 kilometers per hour at several

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.720
points, before finally coming to rest at a
nearby lake.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.550
At which point, it was retrieved by Foundation
personnel.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:17.949
There were two silver linings to this incredibly
strange anomalous incident: The first was,

00:04:17.949 --> 00:04:21.139
as previously alluded to, nobody actually
died.

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:26.080
The second was that, due to the incredible
speeds at which SCP-018 moved, none of the

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.930
civilian witnesses had any idea what they’d
just encountered.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:34.870
As far as anomalous discoveries go, this was
pretty much as close to a win as you can get.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:40.379
But for one ambitious researcher, it was far
more than just a pleasingly non-violent initial

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:46.310
containment story - It was a doorway to improving
the Foundation’s technology as a whole.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:47.840
Meet Dr. Brian Karella.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:53.539
He’s what you might call a maverick, a blue
sky thinker, always on his grind.

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:57.590
The cornerstone of Dr. Karella’s philosophy
was that the Foundation should be making more

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:03.169
active use of its benign anomalies to help
track down and contain their more ornery foes.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:07.650
While everyone else around him seemed to only
see a little rubber nuisance that was better

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:13.279
locked away, Dr. Karella saw the immense potential
in SCP-018.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:18.669
Namely, in providing a vital enhancement to
another piece of Foundation technology: The

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:20.319
SCP-A5 Armor.

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:25.229
It goes without saying that working for the
SCP Foundation is an incredibly dangerous

00:05:25.229 --> 00:05:30.240
job, especially if you’re part of one of
the Foundation’s myriad mobile task forces.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:35.440
The hunt for anomalies can lead to all kinds
of strange and inhospitable terrains.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:41.389
Before it was contained, SCP-096 was famously
captured on an icy, frozen tundra on top of

00:05:41.389 --> 00:05:42.830
a bleak mountain.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:48.559
Because of incidents like this, the Foundation
had first invested money in the SCP-A5 Tactical

00:05:48.559 --> 00:05:49.599
Armor Suit.

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:52.889
Think of them like the Foundation’s answer
to the Iron Man suit.

00:05:52.889 --> 00:05:57.199
However, when dressed in several hundred pounds
of reinforced metal, something important suffers

00:05:57.199 --> 00:05:59.379
along the way: Mobility.

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:03.409
It isn’t exactly easy to lug all that equipment
around.

00:06:03.409 --> 00:06:07.669
And when an anomaly is heading for the hills
at high speeds, being well-defended doesn’t

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:11.509
count for much if you’re already ten miles
behind the target in pursuit.

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:17.550
This, in Dr. Karella’s mind, was exactly
where SCP-018 came into play.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.509
If that little red ball was built into the
foot of an SCP-A5 Armor suit, it could be

00:06:22.509 --> 00:06:26.539
used to bounce the operative wearing it to
tremendous heights.

00:06:26.539 --> 00:06:30.889
This would allow them to not only give chance
against fast-moving anomalies but also cover

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:35.699
difficult terrain and even scale great heights
in a mere instant.

00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:41.470
But it wasn’t just an increase to mobility
that SCP-018 integration offered to the SCP-A5

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:42.470
suit.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:48.130
Picture this: With SCP-108 fused to the sole
of the suit’s reinforced metal foot, lending

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:54.130
it 200% bouncing efficiency, it could unleash
a deadly, concrete-shattering kick.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:57.870
The kind of thing that would leave you singing
in falsetto for the rest of your life if you

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:01.580
were lucky enough to survive it, if you know
what I mean.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.879
To Dr. Karella, it was a match made in heaven.

00:07:03.879 --> 00:07:08.889
It could increase both the mobility and combat
effectiveness of the suits by a considerable

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:09.889
margin.

00:07:09.889 --> 00:07:14.919
And seeing as SCP-018 literally didn’t have
a mind of its own, there’s no way it could

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:20.449
suddenly go rogue during a mission and compromise
everything - just as Able had during his stint

00:07:20.449 --> 00:07:24.740
as a Mobile Task Force operator before they
ran out of targets for him and he started

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.680
slaughtering his own comrades.

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:32.080
Dr. Karella was so confident in the efficacy
of this idea, he contacted the O5 Council

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.699
personally to request approval for this little
pet project.

00:07:35.699 --> 00:07:39.650
This approval was granted, on a purely experimental
basis.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:43.680
The technology would have to prove itself
before being put into common use.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:48.449
It wasn’t exactly what Karella wanted to
hear, but it was a step in the right direction.

00:07:48.449 --> 00:07:53.069
He just needed the perfect opportunity to
put them to the test.

00:07:53.069 --> 00:07:59.490
And then it came: SCP-682, the Infamous Hard
to Destroy Reptile, breached containment.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:03.770
It’d somehow adapted a cloaking ability
and escaped further from the site it was being

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.589
held at than ever before.

00:08:05.589 --> 00:08:10.439
The next time it was spotted was over two
weeks later, causing pandemonium in the Amazon

00:08:10.439 --> 00:08:15.389
Rainforest, devouring tribesmen and wreaking
havoc on the local ecosystem.

00:08:15.389 --> 00:08:20.089
They needed to get on the scene fast and put
that monster down before the damage it caused

00:08:20.089 --> 00:08:25.659
was irreparable, and news of the Beast in
the Amazon leaked out into the local area.

00:08:25.659 --> 00:08:29.749
And thankfully, Dr. Karella had just the tool
for the job.

00:08:29.749 --> 00:08:36.300
Field Agent Hammersmith was fitted with an
SCP-A5 suit, complete with the SCP-018 enhancement

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.729
in his dominant right leg.

00:08:37.729 --> 00:08:43.240
He was dispatched, and immediately, the augmented
suit began to show its efficacy.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:47.680
Agent Hammersmith bounded above the treeline
at incredible speeds, using the HUD in the

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:52.950
suit’s mask to track the heat signature
of SCP-682 moving among the trees below him.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:57.639
He’d been able to bind a tracking collar
to the beast’s neck during an earlier engagement,

00:08:57.639 --> 00:08:59.660
but now the true battle was on.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.899
His heart was pounding, adrenaline coursing
through his veins, but he’d been ensured

00:09:03.899 --> 00:09:08.350
that even 682 would have a hard time tearing
through his suit’s armor.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:13.800
A commander directing him through an earpiece
told him now was the time to engage, before

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.389
682 detected his presence and began developing
countermeasures.

00:09:17.389 --> 00:09:22.571
Dr. Karella was watching a live feed from
the control room, confident that his 018-augmented

00:09:22.571 --> 00:09:24.220
suit would do the job.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:29.230
Following his orders to the letter, Hammersmith
descended down onto 682 from above.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:33.680
However, before he could make contact, the
reptile swiped him with its tail, sending

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.089
his body sailing into a nearby tree.

00:09:36.089 --> 00:09:37.990
However, the suit stood firm.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:41.360
He felt the impact, but the actual damage
was minimal.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.509
Now, it was time for him to face off against
the beast, one on one.

00:09:45.509 --> 00:09:47.660
He didn’t have time to be afraid.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:52.470
As the beast descended upon him, fangs bared,
he gave it a swift kick to the bottom jaw,

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.310
tearing off half of its face.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:59.550
But anyone who knows SCP-682 would tell you
that simply removing its bottom jaw wouldn’t

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.660
even slow 682 down.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.410
It was relentless, attacking Hammersmith with
its fangs and jaws.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:10.680
It tore deep ruts into the suit’s metal,
but the suit was still managing to keep its

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.360
occupant safe.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:14.850
Then Hammersmith struck back.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:20.670
Kick after kick, augmented by the 200% power
of the Super Ball, sliced huge chunks from

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.149
the reptile’s body.

00:10:22.149 --> 00:10:27.870
He kicked in its chest, kicked off limbs,
and with a final mighty kick, even managed

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.720
to bisect the beast in the middle.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:34.970
Of course, even that wouldn’t keep it down
for long, but with the hum of evacuation and

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:40.080
containment helicopters rapidly approaching,
Hammersmith breathed a sigh of relief.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:45.520
Back in the control room, everyone celebrated
- Dr. Karella most of all, vindicated in his

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.329
belief that SCP-018 could save the day.

00:10:49.329 --> 00:10:54.170
And then Agent Hammersmith, without even thinking,
rested his right foot on the floor just that

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.860
little bit too firmly.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:59.100
The sudden bounce sent Hammersmith a mile
into the air.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.930
His Foundation-trained composure evaporated;
all he could do was scream as he blasted up

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.949
into the clouds, then began to plummet.

00:11:06.949 --> 00:11:10.720
Back in the control room, everyone could see
a live feed of Agent Hammersmith hurtling

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:14.529
into a nearby lake and landing with an epic
splash.

00:11:14.529 --> 00:11:19.300
While the regenerating remains of SCP-682
were contained and brought back to the nearest

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:25.509
containment site, another team was sent in
to retrieve the heavily injured Agent Hammersmith.

00:11:25.509 --> 00:11:30.389
His medical examination afterward revealed
he’d suffered two broken legs, seven broken

00:11:30.389 --> 00:11:32.870
ribs, a missing arm, and a skull fracture.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:37.300
If he hadn’t been wearing the suit, his
mangled remains probably would have been devoured

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.620
by the local piranhas by now.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:44.870
But despite that minor hiccup in the plan,
Dr. Karella was still delighted with the results,

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.890
and immensely proud of the little red ball
that could.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:52.360
In his closing remarks on the incident, he
appended a final note to the SCP-018 file,

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:53.360
reading:

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.759
“Don't worry, it's fixed.

00:11:54.759 --> 00:11:56.769
But, I have some more ideas.

00:11:56.769 --> 00:12:02.120
If I can be granted the use of some water
from SCP-006, as well as some other SCPs,

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:07.250
I can deliver you a set of SCP-A5 armor and
an agent that can capture any, if not all,

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.620
rogue or unattained SCPs.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.100
All I'm waiting on is your approval.”

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:18.879
Now go check out “Why Everyone Wants to
Eat this Corpse - SCP-1176” and “SCP-1025

00:12:18.879 --> 00:12:24.060
- Encyclopedia of Common Diseases” for more
anomalous objects that are full of surprises!

